  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nThis PR adds the catalog case `examples/catalog/3d/rough-finish`. It is the first catalog case with a 3D Pocket and a 3D Finish.\r\n\r\n- Model: an original part. It is a 50 x 50 x 8 mm plate with a spherical dome (36 mm base diameter, 10 mm high, top at Z18). The generator `model/gen_rough_finish_obj.py` makes a watertight height-field mesh (1.25 mm grid, 3680 triangles, 86 KB). The script checks each edge before it writes.\r\n- Stock: a 50 x 50 x 22 mm box. Machine: \"3-axis mill\", like `2d/first-part`. Heights: clearance at top of stock + 25 mm, like the 2D cases.\r\n- Tools: `EM-0600-4FL` (rough) and `BN-0600` (6 mm ball, finish). Holder `none`, like the neighbours.\r\n- Operations:\r\n  1. `3D Pocket1` (`EM-0600-4FL`): stepover 3 mm, stepdown 2 mm, stock to leave 0.5 mm, strategy `auto`, helix entry, from the top of stock down to Z8.\r\n  2. `3D Finish Parallel` (`BN-0600`): pattern `parallel`, stepover 1.5 mm, tolerance 0.1 mm, direction angle and pass start at their defaults.\r\n  3. `3D Finish Waterline` (`BN-0600`): pattern `waterline`, tolerance 0.1 mm, stepdown from the scallop law, pass start at its default.\r\n- `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/case_3d_rough_finish.rs` registers the two case tests (`regenerates`, `rebuilds`). `example_catalog.rs` includes it with one line. The file was at 404 lines before this PR, so the module is in its own file.\r\n- `site/content/guide/operations/operations-3d.md`: `cargo xtask catalog` wrote the case link into the generated blocks of the 3D Pocket and 3D Finish sections.\r\n\r\nThe `.camproj` and `.nc` come only from `cargo xtask catalog --case 3d/rough-finish`.\r\n\r\nNo product code changes.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\n- Verifier: `cam.verify()` gives `ok` with no blocking finding. The script stops before the post if it does not.\r\n- Program: 7569 lines, three `(OPERATION: ...)` sections, 246 KB. Project: 3.5 MB.\r\n- Run time in debug, `cargo test --test example_catalog -- catalog_3d_rough_finish --test-threads=1`: `rebuilds` 26.4 s, `regenerates` 25.3 s (budget 60 s).\r\n- The first version used a 1 mm parallel stepover and a 0.05 mm tolerance. It took 39.9 s and 36.3 s. I made the numbers coarser to give more margin in a parallel suite.\r\n\r\n## Bugs that the case shows\r\n\r\nThe pinned program shows the behaviour of today. Each fix makes the program again.\r\n\r\n- #3669: the 3D Pocket applies the stock to leave only sideways. The apex of the dome and the plate get 0 mm; the flanks get 0.21 to 0.38 mm.\r\n- #3670: a re-entry in a level is a straight plunge into stock, although the entry is a helix (about 29 in this program, for example NC lines 126-128).\r\n- #3671: the rapid between two levels goes down to the floor of the last cut with no margin (lowest `G0` at Z10, NC line 1625).\r\n\r\nThe case README names the three bugs. A comment on #2392 links them.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n- `cargo xtask catalog --case 3d/rough-finish`: rebuilt.\r\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: all 15 cases `checked` (`2d/drill-overfeed` as refusal).\r\n- `camcraft-app` test binaries: `example_catalog` (39 passed, 4 ignored), `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `first_part_programs`, `golden_cl`, `conformance`, `docs_troubleshooting`: all green.\r\n- `cargo test -p xtask catalog`: green.\r\n- Site tests that read `operations-3d.md`: `test_guide_refresh`, `test_release_022_guide`, `test_release_026_guide` pass.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- Heavy lanes: not run (no product code change).\r\n- `test_guide_icons`, `test_guide_images`, `test_guide_navigation`: they need `zola`, which is not installed here. `test_guide_icons` also fails for the missing icon `op-waterjet-profile.png`, which this PR does not touch.\r\n- No screenshots of the case. No app window was opened.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Examples: the catalog case `3d/rough-finish` shows a 3D Pocket rough and two 3D Finish operations (Parallel and Waterline) on a domed part.\r\n\r\nEffort: medium\r\n\r\nFixes #2866\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n",
